          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em bundle gerbe
            is a special model for the total space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#BnU1"} circle 2-group
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
            (often taken to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = AUT(H)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+bundle+gerbe"} nonabelian bundle gerbe
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a model for the total space groupoid of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %p
            The definition of
            %em bundle gerbe
            is not in fact a special case (nor a generalization) of the definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong bundle gerbe
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+submersion"} surjective submersion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi π
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Y
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                      \\\
                      X
                      }
            %li
              %p
                together with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi L
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Y
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      L
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                      \\\
                      Y \times_X Y
                      }
              %p
                over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                with itself, i.e.
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi L
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
